morpheus's design draws on public sources:

- Claude Code's memory documentation (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory):
  an index file loaded into every session with topic files read on demand,
  the user, feedback, project and reference memory types, and memory as
  plain markdown that people can read and edit.
- Anthropic's Managed Agents "Dreams" documentation
  (https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/dreams): an offline job
  that reads past sessions and an existing memory store, merges duplicates,
  replaces stale entries, and writes its result for review instead of editing
  the store in place.
- The AIDevCon 2026 London talk on context engineering and dreaming
  (https://tessl.io/registry/ainativedev/aidevcon-2026-ldn/0.100.14/files/talk-lamis-context-engineering-dreaming/transcript.md):
  memory as files searched with ordinary tools, versioning with provenance,
  layered permissions, and a human accepting or rejecting each proposed change.

An early draft was compared against timoncool/dream-skill
(https://github.com/timoncool/dream-skill). morpheus includes no code or text
from it.
